{
  "id": "torque_or_moment_of_force___online_converter",
  "title": "Torque or Moment of Force - Online Converter",
  "description": "Torque or moment - the tendency of a force to rotate an object. Convert between common torque or moment units using the formula T = F × a, where T is torque, F is force, and a is moment arm.",
  "type": "datatable",
  "components": [
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "## Torque or Moment of Force - Online Converter\n\nTorque or moment - the tendency of a force to rotate an object around an axis or a point - is defined as the product of the force and the distance from the point or axis to the force vector.\n\n**Formula:** T = F × a\n\nWhere:\n- **T** = torque or moment of force (Nm, lbf ft)\n- **F** = applied force (N, lbf)\n- **a** = moment arm (m, ft)\n\n### Example - Torque exerted by a Wrench\n\nA force of 250 N is acting at the end of a 30 cm long wrench. The torque exerted:\n\nT = (250 N) × (30 cm) × (0.01 m/cm) = 75 Nm"
    },
    {
      "type": "calculator",
      "headers": [
        "Parameter",
        "Value",
        "Unit"
      ],
      "inputs": [
        {
          "id": "force",
          "label": "Applied Force (F)",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 250,
          "unit": "N"
        },
        {
          "id": "moment_arm",
          "label": "Moment Arm (a)",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 0.3,
          "unit": "m"
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "id": "torque_nm",
          "label": "Torque",
          "formula": "inputs.force * inputs.moment_arm",
          "unit": "Nm",
          "format": "decimal"
        },
        {
          "id": "torque_lbf_ft",
          "label": "Torque",
          "formula": "(inputs.force * inputs.moment_arm) * 0.737562",
          "unit": "lbf ft",
          "format": "decimal"
        },
        {
          "id": "torque_kgf_m",
          "label": "Torque",
          "formula": "(inputs.force * inputs.moment_arm) * 0.101972",
          "unit": "kgf m",
          "format": "decimal"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "datatable",
      "headers": [
        "Torque Unit",
        "Conversion Factor to Nm",
        "Description"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Newton-meter (Nm)",
          "1",
          "SI unit of torque"
        ],
        [
          "Pound-force foot (lbf ft)",
          "1.35582",
          "Imperial unit"
        ],
        [
          "Kilogram-force meter (kgf m)",
          "9.80665",
          "Metric unit"
        ],
        [
          "Dyne-centimeter (dyne cm)",
          "0.00000001",
          "CGS unit"
        ],
        [
          "Pound-force inch (lbf in)",
          "0.112985",
          "Imperial unit"
        ]
      ]
    }
  ]
}